<BaseLayout title="Motor Mounts" description="LS motor mount options for the Hyundai Genesis Coupe: Sikky, LOJ Conversions, and ISR Performance compared, including BK1 vs BK2 fitment.">
  <h1>Motor Mounts</h1>
  <p>
    Engine position sets the tone for the rest of the swap: radiator clearance, header fitment, driveshaft angle, and accessory access.
    Most people use a complete mount kit rather than universal brackets, and stick with the same brand's oil pan and headers so everything lines up.
  </p>

  <div class="note">
    <p><strong>BK1 vs BK2:</strong> the factory 2009–12 (BK1) engine mount uses three studs to the subframe; the 2013–16 (BK2) mount uses a single center stud. Check that the kit you buy covers your chassis. LOJ, for example, designs for BK2 and ships BK1 orders with a drill and washer to modify the subframe.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>The Three Main Kits</h2>
