    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Prices as listed by each vendor in October 2026.</p>

  <h2>Choosing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Plan the whole package, not just mounts.</strong> Mount position decides which oil pan, headers, and driveshaft length you need. Mixing brands is where most fitment headaches come from.</li>
    <li><strong>Urethane vs aluminum bushings:</strong> urethane is the street choice; solid aluminum transfers a lot more vibration into the cabin.</li>
    <li><strong>Keep the steering shaft and fuse box in mind</strong>: header routing around them changes with engine position.</li>
  </ul>

